    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0581" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg493"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grubb to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 252.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to send you the following
                    telegram: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I am authorized to inform you that the prohibition on the importation of
                            American pork into Spain has been taken off.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I received, this morning, information from the Count of Casa Miranda, private
                    secretary to Mr. Canovas, assuring me that the prohibition on the importation of
                    American pork into Spain had been taken off, and that the royal decree,
                    announcing this fact, would be published before the end of this week.</p>
                <p>At 2 o’clock I had an interview with the Duke of Tetuan in the ministry of state,
                    and he also informed me officially of this fact. I may add the duke expressed
                    himself as well pleased with the result of the negotiations, and congratulated
                    me upon the course I had taken in refusing <pb facs="0582" n="494"
                        xml:id="pg494"/> to accept the report of the medical committee, and in
                    taking the matter personally to Mr. Canovas.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy and translation of the argument with which, at the close of my
                    last interview with Mr. Canovas, I furnished him.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Burd Grubb.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d379-a1.xml" xpointer="d379-a1"/>
